lib/shellsdr/libfax.so.1: the FAX weather fax decoder library (radio_fax_decoder,
https://github.com/darauble/radio_fax_decoder), used by the FAX VFO type.

Its decoder core (FaxDecoder.cpp/.h) comes from OpenCPN's weatherfax_pi
(Copyright (C) 2015 by Sean D'Epagnier) via KiwiSDR (Beagle_SDR_GPS) and is
licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later; the rest of
FAX is MIT licensed. The library as a whole is therefore under the GPL v3, and
so is this binary package as a whole, which includes it. The text of the GPL v3
is in GPL-3 beside this file. The source of the library is at the address above.

ShellSDR's own source code is MIT licensed. ShellSDR loads libfax.so.1 at run
time; without it the FAX type is shown as unavailable and everything else works.
